This is the Community Sensor Model base interface library.

Compilation
-----------
The repository now uses GNU autotools for Unix-like builds.  Generate the
build system, configure an install prefix, and build with:

  ./autogen.sh    (if building from a Git clone)
  ./configure --prefix=/path/to/csm3/install/dir
  make
  make install

To compile 32 bit, set the CXXFLAGS environment variable to include "-m32" when running configure:

  CXXFLAGS=-m32 ./configure --prefix=/path/to/csm3/install_32/dir

To stage into a temporary directory instead of the default `/usr/local`, use
the standard `DESTDIR` mechanism during install:

  make install DESTDIR=/tmp/csm-package-root

The build produces the shared `libcsmapi` library and installs headers under
`include/csm`.  To generate API documentation, run:

  make doxygen

If you need ABI compatibility with the historical Linux build that defined
`_GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI=0`, configure with:

  ./configure --enable-legacy-cxx11-abi


Windows
-------
Windows compilation requires the use of Cygwin to provide tools like 'make' and 'perl'.  You should also be sure that Microsoft's Visual C++'s "cl.exe" is in your $PATH and that $INCLUDE and $LIB are set appropriately.  When compiling on Windows, the "all" target does not do the right thing.  Instead build with:

  make -f Makefile.win32 csmapi.dll install clean
